The reports merged into #4471 include two causes. The shared parser reads dates month first even for day-first tenants. The booking-v3 date hint tells people to enter month first while that form reads dates in the tenant's order. These need separate fixes.

## Reports by cause

The table deduplicates report IDs and classifies reports using each tenant's locale and form, rather than intake's browser-based tag. It also notes reports the desk read as one-day moves. Those reports need investigation; their text alone does not establish a third cause.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Queue

The desk continues to receive and merge reports. Compare received and merged weeks before treating a snapshot count as current.

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Triage

Do not merge on subject alone. Look up the tenant and channel, compare the underlying cause, and leave reports without enough evidence unplaced for investigation. The accepted subject-only decision remains a historical record; a replacement decision should be made separately.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
